  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large mason jar over medium heat.",
    "Add the diced onion and cook until softened, about 3 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic and grated ginger and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the cumin, cinnamon, turmeric, salt, and black pepper and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the diced apricots, chicken broth, and honey. Stir to combine.",
    "Bring the mixture to a simmer, then reduce the heat to low and cook, covered, for 20 minutes, or until the apricots are tender.",
    "Stir in the fresh parsley and mint. ",
    "Serve the tagine hot, garnished with a dollop of Greek yogurt and a sprinkle of parsley and mint.",
    "Refrigerate any leftovers for up to 3 days or freeze for up to 2 months.",
    "To serve, reheat the tagine over low heat, stirring occasionally, until warm and bubbly.",
    "Serve hot over couscous or rice, if desired."
  ],
